  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1216 AM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe Monsoon high will weaken further going into Monday down to \nnear 594dam at 500mb, with the upper high centroid shifting east \ninto west central NM. Drier conditions will allow daytime \ntemperatures to rise a couple of degrees across central NM, \nexpanding the moderate to major heat risk east into the ABQ \nMetro. PWATs will continue a slow downtrend Monday, leading to a\nmore paltry round of convection that will favor southern and\neastern areas and be capable of producing strong/erratic wind\ngusts. More of the same on Tuesday followed by a slow uptrend in\nPWATs through the end of the week, bringing improved chances for\nstorms as the Monsoon high drifts toward the Four Corners.\nHowever, there is some model spread with regard the the strength\nand position of the Monsoon high by the end of the work week\nleading lower forecast confidence beyond Wednesday.",
